asr-000568
03:08:22.000 --> 03:08:51.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Relief Allowance, ito po yung PERA. So throughout the budget deliberations ay ni-raise po natin na dapat nang dagdagan ang PERA at nagsabi at malinaw na nag-commit ang [unclear] na sa Miscellaneous Personnel Benefits Fund lump sum ay meron pong 11.78 billion specifically para sa pagdagdag ng PERA, which is good for 500 pesos per month

asr-000569
03:08:52.000 --> 03:09:21.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for the roughly 2 million government employees. However, so napakaganda, well, mixed po 'yan. Magandang balita na may increase pero yung increase na 500 ay kapos po, especially now with 7.2% inflation. However, in General Provision Section 63, Personnel Economic Relief Allowance:

asr-000570
03:09:22.000 --> 03:09:28.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In order to supplement the salaries of government personnel covered by RA No. 6758 as amended,

asr-000571
03:09:29.860 --> 03:09:37.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: personnel economic relief allowance pera in the amount of 2,000 pesos per month.

asr-000572
03:09:37.480 --> 03:09:39.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun pa rin po ang nakalagay, 2,000 pesos per month.

asr-000573
03:09:40.700 --> 03:09:46.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So after discussions with the Chair of Committee on Appropriations,

asr-000574
03:09:46.000 --> 03:09:51.260
