Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, as committed by Secretary Kim De Leon during the deliberations on the general principles

asr-000590
03:11:16.380 --> 03:11:18.980
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: as well as the lump sum funds during the plenary deliberations,

asr-000591
03:11:19.500 --> 03:11:38.940
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: There is an amount, as stated by our distinguished colleague, 11.794 billion pesos out of the 58 billion pesos MPBF that is currently earmarked or targeted for an increase in allowances for government employees.

asr-000592
03:11:38.940 --> 03:12:07.620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The initial discussion is that this may be in the form of a 500 peso increase under PERA. However, upon consulting with the Department of Budget and Management, we were told that there were several options currently being considered as to what shape or form this 11.794 billion will be disbursed for additional allowances for government employees.

asr-000593
03:12:07.620 --> 03:12:29.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, while we are still waiting for the decision of the Executive as to what shape and form this additional allowance will take, I agree with the amendment being proposed by our distinguished colleague in the general provision pertaining to the PERA.

asr-000594
03:12:30.220 --> 03:12:35.540
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Because in its current form, that general provision limits the amount.

asr-000595
03:12:36.040 --> 03:12:37.580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It tags it to be...

asr-000596
03:12:37.620 --> 03:12:47.540
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It tags it to be 2,000 pesos. So that doesn't give us any flexibility once the Executive does decide on the shape or form of this additional allowance.

asr-000597
03:12:48.160 --> 03:12:54.320
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And for that reason, Madam Speaker, the Committee accepts the proposed amendment of our distinguished colleague.

asr-000598
