Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that 25 of them do not have any capital outlay infrastructure allocations for the coming fiscal year.

asr-000617
03:15:17.300 --> 03:15:22.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, that will be my first proposed amendment. Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-000618
03:15:22.900 --> 03:15:24.240
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: What does the sponsor say?

asr-000619
03:15:25.440 --> 03:15:35.620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, last year, the House approved and included in the HGAB a very important special provision as well as very important funding...

asr-000620
03:15:35.620 --> 03:15:37.620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: for the payment of the

asr-000621
03:15:37.620 --> 03:15:38.360
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: deficiency

asr-000622
03:15:38.400 --> 03:15:39.140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: to SUCs,

asr-000623
03:15:39.440 --> 03:15:41.620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: amounting to 12 billion Pesos,

asr-000624
03:15:43.880 --> 03:15:47.120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: 7.5 billion of which will come from the HDF

asr-000625
03:15:47.180 --> 03:15:50.940
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and 4.5 billion of which we included in the HGABA.

asr-000626
03:15:50.940 --> 03:15:53.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I will inform you that I am happy to report, Madam Speaker,

asr-000627
03:15:54.200 --> 03:15:56.140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: that two weeks ago,

asr-000628
03:15:56.140 --> 03:15:59.340
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we conducted a ceremonial turnover

asr-000629
03:15:59.500 --> 03:16:02.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: along with the Commission of Higher Education,

asr-000630
03:16:03.220 --> 03:16:07.200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: with Pa-Suk and the Presidents of Mainland folders of State Universities and Colleges

asr-000631
03:16:07.620 --> 03:16:20.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I believe roughly 99 out of the 113 state universities were all given their checks for the payment of deficiency to SUC.

asr-000632
03:16:20.540 --> 03:16:23.020
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So just that was two weeks ago, Madam Speaker.

asr-000633
03:16:23.300 --> 03:16:29.400
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And a lot of the state university presidents were saying that they would use that additional funding

asr-000634
03:16:29.400 --> 03:16:37.260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: to be able to augment whichever funds they need to fund infrastructure projects and operating expenses.

asr-000635
03:16:37.620 --> 03:16:44.060
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, Madam Speaker, we were also told that out of the 12 billion that we provided for last year,

asr-000636
03:16:44.500 --> 03:16:53.040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: roughly 2.99 billion pesos or 3 billion pesos almost would be unutilized,

asr-000637
03:16:53.040 --> 03:17:02.120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: which means that not the whole 12 billion pesos which we provided for is forecasted to not be utilized this year.

asr-000638
03:17:02.620 --> 03:17:07.500
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Therefore, Madam Speaker, if I may respond,

asr-000639
03:17:07.620 --> 03:17:17.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: our distinguished colleague, that rather than putting in additional funding for these specific state universities and colleges,

asr-000640
03:17:18.020 --> 03:17:24.160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we instead put in a special provision under the Commission on Higher Education,

asr-000641
03:17:24.160 --> 03:17:34.160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: which essentially mandates them to disburse the remaining 2.995 billion pesos that remains unutilized

asr-000642
03:17:34.740 --> 03:17:37.160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: from the amount that we provided for last year.

asr-000643
03:17:37.620 --> 03:17:45.880
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Which is 12 billion pesos for payment of any remaining deficiencies to the state universities and colleges

asr-000644
03:17:45.880 --> 03:17:54.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: that may have been accrued during the school year 2025 and school year 2025 to 2026.

asr-000645
03:17:55.320 --> 03:18:02.740
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, our distinguished colleague mentioned an amount, an amount roughly totaling 700 million pesos.

asr-000646
03:18:02.740 --> 03:18:07.420
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: But this one, Madam Speaker, the counterproposal is to,

asr-000647
03:18:07.620 --> 03:18:15.880
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: to allocate back the 2.995 billion pesos towards addressing any deficiencies

asr-000648
03:18:15.880 --> 03:18:22.420
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: that state universities and colleges may have with regard to the implementation of the free higher education.

asr-000649
03:18:22.420 --> 03:18:32.740
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And with that, Madam Speaker, our distinguished colleague knows how much I support the advocacy in terms of higher education.

asr-000650
03:18:32.740 --> 03:18:36.740
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: In fact, Madam Speaker, aside from the special provision that we put forth,

asr-000653
03:18:38.020 --> 03:18:41.660
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: but that we put into the HGAAB,

asr-000654
03:18:41.840 --> 03:18:51.980
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we also put in 2.1 billion pesos as an additional funding for tertiary education subsidy.

asr-000655
03:18:52.000 --> 03:19:02.900
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: which hopefully would help address the shortfall in the funding under CHED for providing scholarships to college students in need.

asr-000656
03:19:03.080 --> 03:19:13.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: To be precise, Madam Speaker, we put in the 2.1 billion pesos to be able to cater to four-piece beneficiaries that have already enrolled

asr-000657
03:19:13.000 --> 03:19:19.520
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: but are not accounted for in the tertiary education subsidy fund that is there in the NEP.

asr-000658
03:19:19.520 --> 03:19:33.720
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: On top of that, Madam Speaker, we also added 1.77 billion pesos for the Tulong-Dunong program, which currently has zero funding in the NEP.

asr-000659
03:19:34.120 --> 03:19:45.800
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, Madam Speaker, in total, in the House General Appropriations Bill, we put in 2.95 billion pesos for payment of deficiency to SUCs,

asr-000660
03:19:45.800 --> 03:19:49.500
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: 2.1 billion pesos for tertiary education subsidies,

asr-000661
03:19:49.520 --> 03:19:54.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and 1.77 billion pesos for the Tulong-Dunong program.

asr-000662
03:19:54.680 --> 03:20:06.700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And with that, Madam Speaker, given that we have put in a lot of additional funding to cater to the needs of our higher education institutions and students,

asr-000663
03:20:07.180 --> 03:20:10.500
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the committee respectfully rejects the proposed amendment.

asr-000664
03:20:11.520 --> 03:20:12.700
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: What does the House say?

asr-000665
03:20:14.280 --> 03:20:18.160
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, I move to approve the proposed amendment.

asr-000666
03:20:19.520 --> 03:20:25.020
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The session is suspended.

asr-000668
03:20:29.100 --> 03:20:30.060
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session resumed.

asr-000669
03:20:32.520 --> 03:20:36.760
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, I withdraw that motion.

asr-000670
03:20:37.820 --> 03:20:47.780
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: On the part of the House, we join the proponent to disapprove and reject the proposed amendment.

asr-000671
03:20:49.520 --> 03:20:54.340
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The proposed amendment is hereby rejected.

asr-000672
03:20:55.240 --> 03:21:00.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, I have two more amendments that we'd like to propose on the floor.

asr-000673
03:21:00.180 --> 03:21:00.340
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Proceed.

asr-000674
03:21:01.100 --> 03:21:03.380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-000675
03:21:03.920 --> 03:21:11.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next amendment would be in line, actually, to the one already mentioned by our distinguished sponsor.

asr-000676
