asr-000681
03:21:49.520 --> 03:21:53.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to 2027, or even to 2027 to 2028.

asr-000682
03:21:54.080 --> 03:22:04.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And Madam Speaker, good sponsor, my next amendment would be in page 349 of volume 1B

asr-000683
03:22:04.020 --> 03:22:11.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of the General Appropriations Bill, the special provision number 2

asr-000684
03:22:11.640 --> 03:22:16.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: on the use of Higher Education Development Fund for the payment of funding deficiencies

asr-000685
03:22:16.440 --> 03:22:19.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: for the free higher education for state universities and colleges.

asr-000686
03:22:19.520 --> 03:22:30.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In the last sentence, in line 24, we propose that the word may, in the last sentence,

asr-000687
03:22:30.820 --> 03:22:38.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: be replaced with the word shall, to read that the HEDF shall also be used

asr-000688
03:22:38.280 --> 03:22:41.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to cover the current year's FHE deficiencies.

asr-000689
03:22:41.680 --> 03:22:48.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We raise this, Madam Speaker, distinguished sponsor, because it is the report of state universities

asr-000690
03:22:48.700 --> 03:22:49.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and colleges.

asr-000691
03:22:49.520 --> 03:22:56.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It is on the ground that the use of the word may has added difficulty to some SUCs

asr-000692
03:22:56.900 --> 03:23:05.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to accessing the funding already existing to ensure that whatever is already their deficiency

asr-000693
03:23:05.600 --> 03:23:12.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: can be provided already, even if they have already submitted the necessary documentation.

asr-000694
03:23:13.180 --> 03:23:19.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Madam Chair, a simple amendment of the word may,

asr-000695
03:23:19.520 --> 03:23:26.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to shall, in line 24, page 349 of volume 1B of the GAB,

asr-000696
03:23:26.680 --> 03:23:30.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: under the special provision number 2, is the second amendment.

asr-000697
03:23:30.820 --> 03:23:33.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And then my last amendment, Madam Speaker, good sponsor,

asr-000698
03:23:34.060 --> 03:23:41.220
